A||||7||Seanh||Electronic Ignition?||||1||
Z||000000||Seanh||07-20-2000||06:48 PM||||Just wondering, Iv seen these Electronic Igntion kits that say you can put them on in an hour. Has anyone here put electronic ing. on their Fiero? Should I? And are there any disadvantages? Thanks<P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8||||reg||1
Z||000001||batboy||07-20-2000||06:51 PM||||We need more info. Actually, all Fieros already have electronic ignition.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Seanh||07-20-2000||06:58 PM||||Well, Im not sure what more info you need, but here goes. This system replaces your distributor and controles the sparks through a computer device. It says that youll get up to 40% better gas milage and the car starts faster and runs smoother. Im not sure if this is really that much of an upgade. My parents have a 96 Town Car with electronic Ingition system on it, and a 90 without it. The 90 has a larger engine, and the 96 seems to have alot better milage and acceleration with it. Ford says its due in part to the overhead cam. but also the ingiontion system plays a large part.<P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8||||reg||1
Z||000003||StuGood||07-20-2000||07:19 PM||||Either that's an 1890 Town Car, or somebody decided to downgrade things, if the '90 really has a nonelectronic ignition  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> - all U.S. production cars have had electronic ignitions since 1975.  <P>If you mean your parents' car has the aftermarket system you're considering, maybe they'd let you borrow it for a trial period on your Fiero.  <P>Anyway, I bet you won't notice any improvement.  If you really want to upgrade your ignition, maybe you should go with a decent aftermarket ignition coil.     ||||reg||12
Z||000004||DXR_DAD||07-20-2000||08:17 PM||||Just to have a "bolt on" upgrade the MSD Blaster system will do. It's not a multi-spark capactive system  (6A&6AL)<BR>it is a 7.5 amp inductive discharge,= more current= longer spark, add the Blaster coil<BR>a set of good wires and you may see a differance.<P><BR>DXR_DAD||||reg||14
Z||000005||Seanh||07-20-2000||10:47 PM||||We have different Idea about Electronic Ignition system. What Im talking about it a system that doent have a distributor, as most know it. I mean, it still has a "distributor" but no rotor or other internalsf like most cars do. I realize that all cars have electronic Ignition. But I think your understanding what I am talking about. Perhaps I should look into a better coil and new wires. Thanks for the help.<BR>BTW, the system on the 96 is a factory system and I havent worked on it yet, but the 8 spark plug wires split off, 4 go on one cap, and 4 on the other. It a true electronic Ignition system, this is what im talking about.<P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8||||reg||1
Z||000006||gixxer||07-21-2000||02:11 AM||||I think all you are talking about is a "crank trigger" system. No cap or rotor. Lots of cars have this, as do most motorcycles. It uses the crank as the trigger mechanism to send a signal to the ignition black box, the black box chops the power sent to the coil, thus generating a spark. You may notice that there will be one additional spark at the top of the exhaust stroke(which doesn't bother anybody).The coil may be hooked to the spark plug via a plug wire, or, the coil and plug may be essentially one unit, eliminating the plug wire.<BR>The only thing this type of system does is eliminates parts, and is has probably more accuracy in spark timing.<BR>No way on earth are you going to get 40% better fuel milage! maybe just a couple of percent. And thats if it is absolutely dialed in for your engine!<BR>Of course, this is just my opinion.  ||||reg||1
Z||000007||1FST2M6||07-21-2000||08:01 AM||||If your talking about the install of a Crane HI6 or MSD 6AL yes you can install them in about an hour.. there are about 6 wires to hook up and their instructions are really easy to decifer. I've install both and the MSD made the biggest difference in both fuel economy and performance. The Crane unit was ok but the changing of the Crane to the MSD gave me 4lbft of torque with NO other changes.||||reg||1
